{"chunk_id": "6d7caf92ef16", "text": "Arjuna finally confronts Karna on the battlefield. After noticing Karna\u2019s bowstring twang, Arjuna abandons his clash with Aswatthaman and rushes to face his long\u2011time rival. The two exchange bitter taunts: Arjuna recalls Karna\u2019s boastfulness and his silent complicity during Draupadi\u2019s humiliation, vowing that the exile and suffering of the Pandavas will now be avenged. Karna responds with scorn, questioning Arjuna\u2019s past restraint and challenging him to prove his strength in deeds. Their duel erupts in a fierce storm of arrows. Arjuna gradually gains the advantage\u2014cutting Karna\u2019s bow, killing his horses, and finally striking him with a powerful arrow that pierces his armor and leaves him reeling, forcing Karna to flee. Afterward, Arjuna asks to face Bhishma, while his charioteer Uttara confesses terror at the overwhelming violence of the battle.\nArjuna and Karna exchange bitter taunts before a fierce duel in which Arjuna wounds and routs Karna, who briefly loses consciousness and flees.\nThemes: heroic rivalry, vengeance, battle prowess, honor and taunts", "vector": [-0.010532108135521412, -0.02328997105360031, -0.006110767833888531, 0.022686602547764778, -0.009821475483477116, 0.036899250000715256, -0.021305562928318977, -0.004833640996366739, -0.034861210733652115, -0.01701495237648487, 0.00547723239287734, 0.009425935335457325, 0.0023196113761514425, 0.00011470259778434411, 0.006831456441432238, 0.0004039207415189594, 0.04019765555858612, -0.0033637715969234705, 0.025757070630788803, -0.02762080542743206, 0.00012884401076007634, 0.011437159031629562, -0.013180219568312168, 0.02735264226794243, -0.02345086820423603, 0.021895522251725197, 0.0030939325224608183, -0.02716492861509323, 0.002165417419746518, -0.027218559756875038, -0.010733230039477348, -0.0006364684668369591, 0.0008832623716443777, -0.003176057478412986, -0.034861210733652115, 0.013039433397352695, -0.019321154803037643, -0.0331